<title>JAPAN: Hamamatsu Photonics receives order for lasers.</title>
<headline>Hamamatsu Photonics receives order for lasers.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hamamatsu Photonics KK said on Wednesday it had received an order from the Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory of the United States for 400 high-powered laser diode pump alleys.</p>
<p>The alleys, which bundle laser rays, will be used at the laboratory's facility in California.</p>
<p>Delivery of the alleys is expected to start in December 1998, a company statement said.</p>
<p>A Hamamatsu Photonics official said one alley normally costs about $250,000, but the company did not say how much the total order would be worth.</p>
</text>
